{:edb/db-before-t 1928 :edb/db-after-t 1929 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535241 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:15:21.687Z" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197955 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x$." 13194139535241 false] [17592186197955 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x.$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197955 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdzdydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}[∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdz]dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x \\cdot [z]_{z = 0}^{z = 3 - x - y}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x(3 - x - y)dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}[(3x - x^{2})y - \\frac{1}{2}xy^{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(3x - x^{2})(x - 0) - \\frac{1}{2}x(x^{2} - 0)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - x^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx &= [x^{3} - \\frac{3}{8}x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= 8 - 6 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 false] [17592186197955 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x\\cdot [z]_{z=0}^{z=3-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x(3-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3x-{x}^{2})y-\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-{x}^{2})(x-0)-\\frac{1}{2}x({x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =8-6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197963 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y$." 13194139535241 false] [17592186197963 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y.$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197963 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dzdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[x^{2}yz + \\frac{xz^{3}}{3}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y(1 - 0) + x(\\frac{1}{3} - 0)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}[∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3}y + \\frac{1}{6}x^{2}]_{x =-1}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) + \\frac{1}{6}(2^{2} - (-1)^{2}))dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dx &= [\\frac{3y^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y}{2}]_{y = 1}^{y = 2} \\\\\n&= (6 + 1) - (\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 false] [17592186197963 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{[{x}^{2}yz+\\frac{x{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y(1-0)+x(\\frac{1}{3}-0)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})+\\frac{1}{6}({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(6+1)-(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197964 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle  \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186197964 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139535241 false] [17592186197964 1145 "Since the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{π/2}∫_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\sin y}{x}dzdydx &= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}dx∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz &= [\\ln \\mid x \\mid ]_{1}^{2} \\cdot [- \\cos y]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot (4 - 1) \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - \\ln 1) \\cdot (-\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\cos (0)) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - 0) \\cdot (0 + 1) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 3\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2\n$$" 13194139535241 false] [17592186197964 1145 "Since the domain of integration $R = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{x}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{1}^{2}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot (4-1) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0)\\cdot (0+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2.\n$$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186198312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339350 13194139535241 true] [17592186198312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339357 13194139535241 true] [17592186198312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339364 13194139535241 true] [17592186198312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339371 13194139535241 true] [17592186198312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339378 13194139535241 true] [17592186198320 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339315 13194139535241 true] [17592186198320 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339336 13194139535241 true] [17592186198320 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339343 13194139535241 true] [17592186198320 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339385 13194139535241 true] [17592186198321 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339294 13194139535241 true] [17592186198321 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339301 13194139535241 true] [17592186198321 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339308 13194139535241 true] [17592186198321 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339322 13194139535241 true] [17592186198321 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339329 13194139535241 true] [17592186198899 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535241 true] [17592186198899 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186198899 1100 "What is $∫_{0}^{1}∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{2}xy + yz + xzdxdydz$?" 13194139535241 false] [17592186198899 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+z)x+yz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)\\,{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2}+yz[x]_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)(2-0)+yz(2-0)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$, treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(1+z)y+2z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)[{y}^{2}]_{1}^{2}+2z[y]_{1}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)(4-1)+2z(2-1))\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3(1+z)+2z)\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z & ={[3z+\\frac{5}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3(1-0)+\\frac{5}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339295 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1089 "q-161268" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1100 "${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1113 #uuid "3f5e6d22-78e1-5ce4-8774-243957052edf" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339294 1145 "Since the domain of integration $R=[-1,2]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]\\times [-1,-\\frac{1}{2}]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz & =[{x}^{2}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{-1}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339296 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339297 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339298 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339299 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339300 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1041 "selection" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339298 13194139535241 true] [17592186339295 1110 #uuid "49ebd11c-67c5-503d-82af-d77c05c7da2d" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339296 1034 "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535241 true] [17592186339296 1111 #uuid "bf0dd2b6-4b08-5b1a-8cc5-947c37241514" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339297 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535241 true] [17592186339297 1111 #uuid "57c1813d-68d4-53cd-92ac-a20c8da44331" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339298 1034 "3" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535241 true] [17592186339298 1111 #uuid "bee916ac-becc-5fd6-8660-d1341a4b5669" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339299 1034 "1" 13194139535241 true] [17592186339299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535241 true] [17592186339299 1111 #uuid "bab21f6e-1100-524b-921f-3ef0f21225f3" 13194139535241 true]